        "LineNumber":  1024,
        "Line":  "**Also verified:** Both JWT engines require the full claim set (`require: [...]`) including `exp`, `nbf`, `iat`, `iss`, `aud`, `sub`, `jti`, and explicitly enable `verify_signature`, `verify_exp`, `verify_nbf`, `verify_iat`, `verify_iss`, `verify_aud`. `leeway=0` in the customer JWT service disallows clock skew tolerance (a defensible strict choice for 15-minute tokens). Customer and admin JWTs use **separate signing keypairs**, separate `iss`/`aud` values (`\"RealityTunnel Billing/Auth\"`/`\"RealityTunnel Client\"` vs `\"RealityTunnel Admin\"`/`\"RealityTunnel Admin Panel\"`), and separate verification code paths (`get_current_account` vs `get_current_admin` in `dependencies.py`), so a customer token presented to an admin endpoint (or vice versa) fails at the `iss`/`aud` validation step inside `jwt.decode`. **Cross-token-type confusion is not possible.**",
